149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 358 0 R
/E (Idea: gene expression \(RNA\) and DNA accessibility \(ATAC\) are not the same kind of signal, so we stop mixing them together early. A gene can only be regulated if \(a\) its DNA region is open/accessible, and \(b\) it is co-expressed with the TF, these are two separate checks, not one blended score.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 359 0 R
/E (RNA side: a small neural network turns each gene's expression pattern \(mean, variability, how often it's detected, plus a 50-number "co-expression fingerprint"\) into an embedding.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 360 0 R
/E (ATAC side: a similarly small network turns each gene's accessibility pattern into its own embedding.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 361 0 R
/E (Both sides talk to their gene neighbors using a graph neural network, so each gene also learns from nearby co-expressed genes and candidate TF targets.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
