/E (Splitting rule: every unique TF-gene pair is assigned to train/validation/test once, globally, before being divided up per tier. This guarantees a pair can never be "training data" in one tier and "test data" in another, so the zero-shot test on dual-evidence is genuinely fair.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
